# Shell scripts must arrive with LF, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true at the SYSTEM level by default, so a Windows checkout
# writes CRLF into the working tree while HEAD keeps LF — and `git status` still reports a clean
# tree from the Windows side, so nothing looks wrong. Bash then refuses the file outright: measured
# 2026-08-14 on a real rig, scripts/selftest.sh died with "set: -: invalid option" and a run of
# $'\r' errors. The documented install route is not affected — `claude plugin install` runs inside
# the distro, so the files arrive with LF — but a repository checkout made on Windows (a
# contributor's path, or anyone running scripts/selftest.sh from such a clone) is. See issue #41.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Keep the UTF-8 BOM in PowerShell recipes as ordinary content for Windows PowerShell 5.1.
*.ps1 -text
